# The map sibling of reject/arr_type_as_value: `[string: int]` is the TYPE
# spelling, and the empty-map literal is `[]string: int`. Guessing the type
# spelling is the natural mistake and used to report "expected an expression".
# expect: is the TYPE, not a value
# expect: []string: int
fn main():
    m := [string: int]
    println(str(len(m)))
